@startuml iterator_logistics
title Iterator (logistics): recorrer las rutas de un corredor sin conocer su anidación
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam roundCorner 0
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FDF3EE
  BorderColor #444444
  ArrowColor #444444
}
hide empty members

abstract class RouteComponent <<Component>> {
  + {abstract} total_distance_km(): float
  + {abstract} describe(): str
}

class SingleRoute <<Leaf>>

class RouteCorridor <<Aggregate>> {
  - _children: list[RouteComponent]
  + children: tuple[RouteComponent, ...]
  + add(component): None
  + __iter__(): RouteLeafIterator
}

class RouteLeafIterator <<Iterator>> {
  - _pending: list[RouteComponent]
  + __iter__(): RouteLeafIterator
  + __next__(): RouteComponent
}

class "POST /logistics/corridors" as Endpoint <<Client>>

SingleRoute -up-|> RouteComponent
RouteCorridor -up-|> RouteComponent
RouteCorridor o--> RouteComponent : hijos
RouteCorridor ..> RouteLeafIterator : crea
RouteLeafIterator --> RouteComponent : entrega hojas
Endpoint --> RouteCorridor : for leaf in corridor

note right of RouteLeafIterator
  Recorrido en profundidad con pila propia:
  dos recorridos del mismo corredor
  no se interfieren.
end note
@enduml
